        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(extensions/huggingface): bound model discovery JSON response read to prevent OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`discoverHuggingfaceModels` called `response.json()` directly on the Hugging Face `/models` endpoint, buffering the entire payload. A huge or runaway response could OOM the process before model discovery finishes.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace the unbounded `response.json()` call with `readProviderJsonResponse` (already used by OpenRouter OAuth and other bounded-read fixes). The response is now capped at 16 MiB; anything larger falls back to the static catalog, matching the existing fallback behavior for non-OK responses.\n\n## User Impact\n\nModel discovery for the Hugging Face provider is resilient to unexpectedly large API responses.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Regression test added in `extensions/huggingface/models.test.ts`: stubs `fetch` with a >16 MiB JSON body and asserts the function returns the static catalog instead of crashing.\n- Local verification:\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/huggingface/models.test.ts` passes.\n  - `OPENCLAW_OXLINT_SKIP_PREPARE=1 node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs extensions/huggingface/models.ts extensions/huggingface/models.test.ts` passes.\n",
        "branch": "fix/huggingface-models-json-response-bound",
